                "text": "I'm examining the interior 7x8 training region and noticing the output forms alternating bands of 2s and 4s that shift per row, almost like a striped filling pattern replacing the extra 3 anomaly.\n\nNow I'm testing whether these bands radiate from the seed cell as concentric L-shapes, checking if the Chebyshev distance from the seed at (3,6) determines the color of each cell.\n\nWait, I need to relocate the seed\u2014it's actually at (6,4), not where I assumed, since col3 is the border and col4 starts the interior. So the true center is row6, col4, and the band formula becomes max(|r-6|,|c-4|), coloring 3 for band 0, 4 for odd bands, 2 for even bands. I'm recomputing each cell across rows3-9 and cols4-10 under this corrected center.",
